{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function throttleStrategy(options): ThrottleStrategy;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/strategies/throttleStrategy.ts#L47","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/strategies/throttleStrategy.ts:47"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a throttle strategy that ensures transactions are evenly spaced\nover time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides smooth, controlled execution patterns ideal for UI updates like\nsliders, progress bars, or scroll handlers where you want consistent\nexecution timing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ThrottleStrategyOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThrottleStrategyOptions"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration for throttle behavior"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ThrottleStrategy.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThrottleStrategy"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A throttle strategy instance"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Throttle slider updates to every 200ms\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  onMutate: (volume) => {\n    settingsCollection.update('volume', draft => { draft.value = volume })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.updateVolume(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: throttleStrategy({ wait: 200 })\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"code","value":"// Throttle with leading and trailing execution\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  onMutate: (data) => {\n    collection.update(id, draft => { Object.assign(draft, data) })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: throttleStrategy({\n    wait: 500,\n    leading: true,\n    trailing: true\n  })\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction throttleStrategy(options): ThrottleStrategy;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/strategies/throttleStrategy.ts:47](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/strategies/throttleStrategy.ts#L47)\n\nCreates a throttle strategy that ensures transactions are evenly spaced\nover time.\n\nProvides smooth, controlled execution patterns ideal for UI updates like\nsliders, progress bars, or scroll handlers where you want consistent\nexecution timing.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`ThrottleStrategyOptions`](../interfaces/ThrottleStrategyOptions.md)\n\nConfiguration for throttle behavior\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ThrottleStrategy`](../interfaces/ThrottleStrategy.md)\n\nA throttle strategy instance\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n// Throttle slider updates to every 200ms\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  onMutate: (volume) => {\n    settingsCollection.update('volume', draft => { draft.value = volume })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.updateVolume(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: throttleStrategy({ wait: 200 })\n})\n```\n\n```ts\n// Throttle with leading and trailing execution\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  onMutate: (data) => {\n    collection.update(id, draft => { Object.assign(draft, data) })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: throttleStrategy({\n    wait: 500,\n    leading: true,\n    trailing: true\n  })\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: throttleStrategy\ntitle: throttleStrategy\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction throttleStrategy(options): ThrottleStrategy;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/strategies/throttleStrategy.ts:47](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/strategies/throttleStrategy.ts#L47)\n\nCreates a throttle strategy that ensures transactions are evenly spaced\nover time.\n\nProvides smooth, controlled execution patterns ideal for UI updates like\nsliders, progress bars, or scroll handlers where you want consistent\nexecution timing.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`ThrottleStrategyOptions`](../interfaces/ThrottleStrategyOptions.md)\n\nConfiguration for throttle behavior\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ThrottleStrategy`](../interfaces/ThrottleStrategy.md)\n\nA throttle strategy instance\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\n// Throttle slider updates to every 200ms\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  onMutate: (volume) => {\n    settingsCollection.update('volume', draft => { draft.value = volume })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.updateVolume(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: throttleStrategy({ wait: 200 })\n})\n```\n\n```ts\n// Throttle with leading and trailing execution\nconst mutate = usePacedMutations({\n  onMutate: (data) => {\n    collection.update(id, draft => { Object.assign(draft, data) })\n  },\n  mutationFn: async ({ transaction }) => {\n    await api.save(transaction.mutations)\n  },\n  strategy: throttleStrategy({\n    wait: 500,\n    leading: true,\n    trailing: true\n  })\n})\n```\n"}
